From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 03:58:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: s2r: pass the boot firmware's wake hold
 requests

A suspend-to-RAM on the J604 ends in a cold boot shortly after the wake,
and nothing on either side of the warm boot path can print. m1n1 (the
J604 build) now takes three bring-up requests in the mailbox flags that
mark how far a wake got by the time of the watchdog reset that follows:
bit 5 holds on entering the warm path (30 s watchdog), bit 6 holds right
before the branch to cpu_resume (60 s), bit 7 branches with a 90 s
watchdog armed instead of stopped.

Let warm_flags carry them. The syscore resume already stops the
watchdog first thing when the sleep armed it (wdt_timeout), so pass bit
7 only then; otherwise a successful resume would still be reset.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c
index 132a5b2923..18cc96715f 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c
@@ -152,9 +152,16 @@ struct apple_s2r_mailbox {
 /* Bring-up: the firmware reboots through the watchdog instead of resuming */
 #define S2R_FLAG_REBOOT_AT_ENTRY	BIT_ULL(3)
 #define S2R_FLAG_REBOOT_AT_BRANCH	BIT_ULL(4)
+/* Bring-up: hold with the watchdog armed, or resume with it armed */
+#define S2R_FLAG_HOLD_AT_ENTRY		BIT_ULL(5)
+#define S2R_FLAG_HOLD_AT_BRANCH		BIT_ULL(6)
+#define S2R_FLAG_WDT_THROUGH		BIT_ULL(7)
 #define S2R_FLAGS_OS		(S2R_FLAG_CPUFREQ_INIT | S2R_FLAG_MCC_INIT | \
 				 S2R_FLAG_REBOOT_AT_ENTRY | \
-				 S2R_FLAG_REBOOT_AT_BRANCH)
+				 S2R_FLAG_REBOOT_AT_BRANCH | \
+				 S2R_FLAG_HOLD_AT_ENTRY | \
+				 S2R_FLAG_HOLD_AT_BRANCH | \
+				 S2R_FLAG_WDT_THROUGH)
 #define S2R_FLAG_RESUMED	BIT_ULL(63)
 
 /*
@@ -531,7 +538,7 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(enable, "Offer suspend-to-RAM (\"deep\" mem sleep) when the boo
 
 static ulong warm_flags;
 module_param(warm_flags, ulong, 0644);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(warm_flags, "Warm boot requests to the boot firmware: bit 1 CPU cluster frequency init, bit 2 memory cache init; for bring-up, bit 3 reboot on entering the warm boot path, bit 4 reboot right before resuming (default: 0)");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(warm_flags, "Warm boot requests to the boot firmware: bit 1 CPU cluster frequency init, bit 2 memory cache init; for bring-up, bit 3 reboot on entering the warm boot path, bit 4 reboot right before resuming, bit 5 hold on entering it with a 30 s watchdog, bit 6 hold right before resuming with a 60 s watchdog, bit 7 resume with a 90 s watchdog that the resume stops (needs wdt_timeout) (default: 0)");
 
 static uint skip;
 module_param(skip, uint, 0644);
@@ -678,6 +685,10 @@ static int apple_s2r_finish(unsigned long arg)
 	struct apple_s2r_mailbox *mb = s2r->mailbox;
 	u64 flags = S2R_FLAG_QUIET | (warm_flags & S2R_FLAGS_OS);
 
+	/* Only the resume of an armed sleep stops the watchdog again */
+	if (!s2r->wdt_armed)
+		flags &= ~S2R_FLAG_WDT_THROUGH;
+
 	WRITE_ONCE(mb->entry, cpu_to_le64(__pa_symbol(cpu_resume)));
 	WRITE_ONCE(mb->arg, 0);
 	WRITE_ONCE(mb->flags, cpu_to_le64(flags));
